# EXERCISE ONTOLOGY

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

The Exercise Ontology defines what an exercise is inside the Combat Athlete System.

It does not describe individual exercises.

It defines the universal structure shared by every exercise stored in the Exercise Knowledge Base.

Every exercise must follow this ontology.

This ensures consistency, explainability and interoperability across all CAS engines.

---

# Definition

An exercise is not merely a movement.

An exercise is a structured intervention designed to produce one or more specific adaptations.

Every exercise possesses intrinsic properties that remain constant,

and contextual properties that depend on the athlete.

CAS distinguishes between these two categories.

---

# Scientific Role

The ontology provides the common language used by:

Exercise Knowledge Engine

Decision Engine

Capability Selection Engine

Session Generation Engine

Recovery Engine

Safety Engine

Explainability Engine

Without a common ontology,

these engines cannot reason consistently.

---

# Exercise Identity

Every exercise possesses a unique identity.

Mandatory attributes include:

Exercise ID

Official Name

Alternative Names

Category

Description

Movement Pattern

Exercise Family

---

# Classification

Exercises are classified by multiple dimensions.

Examples include:

Movement Pattern

Primary Physical Capability

Secondary Physical Capabilities

Sport Specificity

Equipment

Technical Complexity

Energy System

No single classification is sufficient.

---

