---

# Evidence

Scientific evidence is documented.

Fields include:

Evidence Level

Scientific Consensus

Research Quality

Practical Consensus

Expert Agreement

Scientific References

CAS distinguishes evidence from opinion.

---

# Explainability

Every property stored in the ontology may later be used by the Explainability Engine.

Example:

Trap Bar Deadlift selected because it preserves the desired force adaptation while reducing lumbar loading compared with the conventional deadlift.

Explainability depends directly on ontology quality.

---

# Evolution

The ontology is expected to evolve continuously.

New properties may be introduced.

Existing properties may be refined.

Backward compatibility should be preserved whenever possible.

---

# Guiding Principles

The ontology should be:

Scientifically grounded.

Internally consistent.

Technology independent.

Extensible.

Explainable.

Compatible with every CAS engine.

No property should exist unless it can improve decision quality.

---

# Final Principle

Exercises are not stored as names.

They are stored as knowledge.

The richer the ontology,

the more intelligent the Combat Athlete System becomes.